From 1b771fbda8f38b765f35f4d858c890c3ead6ff11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:29:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Settings > Network: hotspot, Ethernet, LTE, internet sharing

A Network tab for the Ozark OS network settings, all read and changed
through the ozark-net command:
- Hotspot (wireless Android Auto): name, password, band, country, and
  sharing the radio's internet with devices on it. A new name or password
  is also handed to OpenAuto, so phones get it without a restart.
- Ethernet: automatic (DHCP) or static address, gateway and DNS.
- LTE (ModemManager): on/off, APN, SIM PIN; status shows the carrier,
  technology, signal and address.
Status refreshes every 3 s while the tab is on screen.

TextEntry and Keyboard: text settings on a touchscreen with no physical
keyboard. A TextEntry shows its value; tapping it opens a dialog with an
on-screen keyboard (letters with shift, numbers and symbols).
